\f0\b\fs48 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Architectural Framework for the "Recursive Scientist": Advancing Automated Scientific Discovery via Simulation-Based Inference and Large Language Models\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 The pursuit of automated scientific discovery has entered a transformative paradigm, shifting from the deployment of static machine learning algorithms for predictive analytics to the engineering of autonomous, agentic systems capable of orchestrating the entire research lifecycle. Current taxonomies categorize the integration of Large Language Models (LLMs) into scientific workflows across three tiers of autonomy: from Level 1 systems serving as analytical tools under direct human supervision, to Level 3 frameworks operating as independent scientists capable of generating hypotheses, executing experimental protocols, and drafting academic manuscripts. A high-profile instantiation of a Level 3 system, the "AI Scientist" architecture, demonstrated the capacity to autonomously generate machine learning research by iteratively modifying training scripts, executing computational runs, and synthesizing the outputs into formal papers.\
However, rigorous empirical evaluations of these initial autonomous frameworks have exposed profound architectural and methodological vulnerabilities. Systems relying on unstructured code generation frequently exhibit a severe lack of deep methodological rigor, often producing underdeveloped concepts or logically flawed experimental outcomes. Investigations into unstructured LLM-driven experimental execution reveal critical robustness failures; in several controlled studies, up to forty-two percent of proposed experiments failed entirely due to syntax errors, while successful iterations yielded minimal substantive adaptations, averaging a mere eight percent addition of characters per cycle. Furthermore, such architectures exhibit a marked susceptibility to hallucinating empirical results and generating inaccurate citations, demonstrating an inability to critically assess their own outputs or grasp the intellectual lineage requisite for genuine scientific contribution.\
To transcend the limitations of unstructured text and code generation, the paradigm must shift toward formalized, probabilistically bounded search mechanisms. The proposed "Recursive Scientist" framework represents a critical architectural maturation. By explicitly decoupling the generative creativity of the LLM from the underlying mathematical execution engine, the architecture constrains the LLM's hypotheses within a rigorously defined interface. This structural imposition forces the computational agent to interact exclusively with executable mathematical abstractions\'97such as Ordinary Differential Equations (ODEs), Stochastic Differential Equations (SDEs), and Agent-Based Models (ABMs)\'97rather than generating brittle, monolithic python scripts. When coupled with Simulation-Based Inference (SBI) powered by high-performance compilation frameworks like JAX, this architecture recasts automated scientific discovery not as a stochastic text-generation problem, but as a formal Bayesian inference task over an infinite space of executable mechanistic models.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 Refinement of the Proposed Architecture\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 The foundation of the "Recursive Scientist" relies on a meticulously designed directory structure and a robust discovery loop. The initially proposed architecture provides a strong conceptual baseline but requires significant technical refinement to achieve the stability and scalability necessary for autonomous, closed-loop discovery.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Enhancing the Directory Structure and Interface Design\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 The proposed separation of concerns into \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 core/\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 backends/\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 agents/\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 , and \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 workspace/\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  directories effectively modularizes the pipeline. However, to achieve true autonomy and prevent the hallucination cascades observed in earlier frameworks , the architecture must be expanded to include explicit mechanisms for knowledge retrieval, provenance tracking, and surrogate modeling.\
The \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 core/base_model.py\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  implementation is the linchpin of the system. The requirement for the \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 Scientist Agent\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  to switch seamlessly between ODEs, SDEs, or ABMs necessitates a highly generic yet strictly typed interface. The proposed abstract \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 BaseModel\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  class must enforce structural identifiability.\
